# Build-context excludes for the ONLY image in this repo: the contained
# repro-execution sandbox (.github/repro-exec/Dockerfile, #145 part 3/3).
#
# That Dockerfile bakes NO app code — it only does `FROM ... && apt-get` and the
# repo is bind-mounted read-only at /work at RUNTIME. So this file's job is to keep
# the build CONTEXT sent to the daemon small and clean: never ship the git history,
# the huge node_modules tree, or the fetch-phase's generated specs (which are
# derived from DB findings) into the docker build context.
#
# `docker build ... .` uses the repo root as the context, so this root
# .dockerignore is where the classic builder looks. There is exactly one Dockerfile
# in the repo, so these excludes affect only that sandbox build.
.git
**/node_modules

# The fetch phase writes apps/web/repro-specs.json (derived from DB findings +
# model-generated repros). The sandbox image must never carry it — it is provided
# at runtime via the read-only /work mount, and it must not leak into an image
# layer.
apps/web/repro-specs.json

# Never bake local env / secrets files into the build context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
